message: "If you use this formalization or paper, please cite this work and the underlying asymptotic theorem (Divoux & Wang, 2026)."
type: software
title: "Non-algebraicity of the Extremal Hamiltonian Path Sequence and Formula Restrictions"
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Xingchen"
    affiliation: "School of Mathematics, Sichuan University"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
url: "https://github.com/LStar404/tournament-impossibility"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: "Bilingual paper and Lean 4 formalization for extremal Hamiltonian path counts in tournaments. Spectral moment comparison and a positive log-ratio expansion yield a uniform normalized maximum error O(1/n) about cosh(1)/cos(1), and raw score energy O(n) for maximizers. The actual sequence encoding is connected to this asymptotic without an external graph-asymptotic premise. Formal non-algebraicity and normalized non-q-regularity applications retain FourExponentialIndependence as an explicit input. Raw path counts have no exponential upper bound without that input. Actual all-order expansions, the common jump condition, Condition R and extremizer classification remain unproved."
